WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640
Welcome to our training "Understand Your Account Health Metrics".

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.760
When your business operates at a high standard, you create a seamless shopping experience

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.400
for customers.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.520
Account health metrics can help you measure and improve the customer experience and know

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.040
how well you're complying with our selling policies.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.640
In this training, we'll provide an overview of account health metrics and share tips

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.240
for maintaining a healthy account.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.280
The first step toward achieving a healthy account is understanding our guidelines and

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.520
targets.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:36.240
We encourage you to regularly monitor your account performance using the Account Health

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.660
Dashboard in Seller Central.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.760
From there, you can easily see if you're meeting our performance targets like complying

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.800
with Amazon's policies and maintaining a low, late shipment rate.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.680
Start by signing into your Seller Central account.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.880
To access your Account Health Dashboard, click the menu in the top left corner of the page.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.520
Hover over performance and select "Account Health".

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.680
Three categories determine your overall account health, customer service performance, policy

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.400
compliance, and shipping performance.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:12.040
When you maintain your performance targets across each of these areas, you help create

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:16.920
a great customer experience and set your business up for success.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.320
The customer service performance section helps you measure how satisfied your customers are

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.240
with the products and service you provide.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.080
This metric is determined by your account's Order Defect Rate or ODR.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:34.760
An order has a defect if it results in negative feedback, an A to Z guarantee claim that isn't

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.080
denied, or a chargeback claim.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.720
Let's take a closer look at each of these factors.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.940
Customer feedback is considered negative if the customer leaves a product review of two

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.880
stars or less.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.760
Whether positive or negative, customer feedback is an important part of the Amazon shopping

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.560
experience.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:58.440
Managed appropriately, these reviews can benefit both you and your customers.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:03.280
For example, they may help you quickly identify and address a problem with a product listing

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.560
before your business is negatively impacted.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:12.120
An A to Z guarantee claim allows customers to ask Amazon to investigate a dispute related

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.640
to an order.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:18.360
They can submit a claim if they feel you haven't properly addressed their negative experience

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.560
according to your or Amazon's policies.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:27.160
A to Z guarantee claims help us regain valuable customer trust when the condition of a product

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.320
or the timing of its delivery didn't meet expectations.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:37.120
We recommend following these tips to help prevent negative feedback and claims.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.560
Accurately represent your products using clear images and descriptions.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.000
Accurately describe the condition of your products.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.320
For example, if a customer expects to receive a new item in its original packaging, getting

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:55.320
a used item in excellent condition would still result in a negative customer experience.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.520
Confirm your shipments in seller central as soon as you ship an order.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.280
Cancel out of stock orders and contact customers to let them know you can't fulfill their orders.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:11.560
Respond to customer messages within 24 hours and do your best to resolve any issues.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:15.480
The last metric that impacts your ODR is chargeback claims.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:21.320
A chargeback is when the order amount is refunded to the customer due to a dispute or return.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:26.480
To help avoid chargeback claims, fulfill orders with care by using adequate packaging and

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.680
trackable shipping methods.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:35.120
Your overall ODR target should be less than 1% of total orders during a given 60-day period.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:40.960
For example, if you received 300 orders over the past 60 days, you should aim to receive

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:47.080
less than 3, 1, or 2-star ratings, A to Z guarantee claims, or chargeback claims.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:51.560
The policy compliance section is designed to bring awareness to intellectual property

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:57.480
issues, authenticity concerns, product conditions, and other policy violations.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:02.600
The policies listed in this category help us make the Amazon store safe for buyers and

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.320
fair to all selling partners.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:11.160
Use the seller central search bar to find and review help pages related to these policies.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.880
As a reminder, these resources are provided as informational guides.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:19.640
They aren't comprehensive and don't take the place of legal advice.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:25.360
It's your responsibility to carefully review our policies and your local state and federal

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.960
laws to make sure your products and listings are compliant.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.280
Monitor the policy compliance section of your account health dashboard regularly and

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:37.280
respond to policy violation warnings.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:42.600
For example, if you receive a warning regarding an intellectual property rights violation,

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:47.960
you might follow the appeals process by providing invoices from a valid supply source with other

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.000
relevant documents.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.760
Any documentation requests will appear on your account health dashboard under the Product

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.840
Compliance Request section.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:02.040
Your policy compliance target should be zero, meaning you should aim to avoid all policy

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.640
violations.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:07.840
The shipping performance metric can help you make sure you're giving customers the information

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:11.000
they need after they place an order.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:15.720
The late shipment rate metric represents the total percentage of orders that you confirmed

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.560
after the order's expected shipping date.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:23.400
As a reminder, confirming a shipment in seller central is a separate task from shipping the

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.400
order.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:28.560
For example, a customer orders one of your products, which you've indicated will ship

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.400
within three days.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:34.880
You ship the order within this timeframe, but you wait until four days after the order

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:38.800
was placed to confirm the shipment in seller central.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.120
Since the shipment is confirmed outside of the specified date range, this order is considered

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.600
a late shipment.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:50.320
The pre-fulfillment cancel rate represents the total percentage of orders you canceled

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:52.880
during a given seven-day period.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:57.880
This metric includes all orders or items that you cancel, but doesn't include cancellation

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:03.320
requests initiated by the customer using the order cancellation options in their Amazon

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.720
account.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:10.880
We recommend you keep your available inventory up-to-date to help avoid order cancellations.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:15.280
Your customers depend on tracking numbers to find out where their orders are and when

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.360
they can expect to receive them.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:23.360
The valid tracking rate metric, or VTR, represents the total percentage of packages with a valid

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.880
tracking number during a given 30-day period.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.960
When you confirm a shipment, you'll need to provide the name of the carrier, type of

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:34.700
delivery service you're using, and the tracking ID.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:39.280
Certain orders are excluded from this metric, like audiobook orders that a carrier can't

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:40.880
physically ship.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.480
For included orders, we recommend choosing a carrier that reports tracking information

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:48.000
to Amazon.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:53.240
You can either use our buy shipping services or use one of our integrated carriers.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:56.280
Follow these steps to access the buy shipping page.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.280
1.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:00.320
Select the menu in the top left corner of Seller Central.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:01.320
2.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.080
Hover over orders and select Manage Orders.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.080
3.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:08.640
Click the buy shipping button next to the order you want to ship.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:13.920
If you'd like to find a list of our integrated carriers, type "valid tracking rate FAQ"

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.200
in the Seller Central search bar.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:21.260
For MFN orders or orders you fulfill yourself, your shipping performance targets should be

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:24.680
to keep your late shipment rate below 4%.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:31.840
Your pre-fulfillment cancel rate below 2.5% and VTR above 95%.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:36.720
Fulfillment by Amazon Orders or FBA Orders don't impact your shipping performance or

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:38.600
overall account health.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:44.240
Remember, maintaining your account health targets can help create a great customer experience,

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:48.960
as well as help prevent your selling privileges from being negatively impacted.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:54.280
Along with the information you learned today, we recommend you take a few additional steps

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:59.160
to help maintain your account health and avoid interruption to your business.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:03.960
Check your account health performance at least once a week and as often as possible.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:08.400
Track, ship, and deliver orders on time and as promised.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:12.880
Set a schedule to review your product catalog and remove any restricted products from your

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.280
listings.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:19.880
As a reminder, Amazon policies and your local regulations may change over time.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:25.440
Finally, respond to customer messages within 24 hours and consider using the Amazon Seller

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:29.800
app to respond as soon as possible and from almost anywhere.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:34.600
You can install the Amazon Seller app on your mobile device and log in using your Seller

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:36.880
Central login credentials.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:41.440
You now have the tools to help you maintain a healthy Seller Central account and create

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:43.880
a great customer experience.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:47.760
This concludes our training Understand Your Account Health metrics.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:50.400
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon Store.
